<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#29d6cded42b7f611a09359701e2efaca>
        a               sh:PropertyShape ;
        rdfs:label      "est distinct spatio-temporellement de"@fr , "This symmetric property associates two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume that have no extents in common. If only the fuzzy boundaries of the instances of E92 Spacetime Volume overlap, this property cannot be determined from observation alone and therefore should not be applied. However, there may be other forms of justification that the two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume must not have any of their extents in common regardless of where and when precisely.\nIf this property holds for two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume then it cannot be the case that P132 spatiotemporally overlaps with also holds for the same two instances. Furthermore, there are cases where neither P132 spatiotemporally overlaps with nor P133 is spatiotemporally separated from holds between two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume. This would occur where only an overlap of the fuzzy boundaries of the two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume occurs and no other evidence is available.\nThis property is not transitive. This property is symmetric. This property is irreflexive."@en , "is spatiotemporally separated from"@en ;
        sh:class        cidoc-crm:E92_Spacetime_Volume ;
        sh:description  "This symmetric property associates two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume that have no extents in common. If only the fuzzy boundaries of the instances of E92 Spacetime Volume overlap, this property cannot be determined from observation alone and therefore should not be applied. However, there may be other forms of justification that the two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume must not have any of their extents in common regardless of where and when precisely.\nIf this property holds for two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume then it cannot be the case that P132 spatiotemporally overlaps with also holds for the same two instances. Furthermore, there are cases where neither P132 spatiotemporally overlaps with nor P133 is spatiotemporally separated from holds between two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume. This would occur where only an overlap of the fuzzy boundaries of the two instances of E92 Spacetime Volume occurs and no other evidence is available.\nThis property is not transitive. This property is symmetric. This property is irreflexive."@en ;
        sh:name         "is spatiotemporally separated from"@en , "est distinct spatio-temporellement de"@fr ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:path         cidoc-crm:P133_is_spatiotemporally_separated_from .

<https://astrea.linkeddata.es/shapes#661c46c5e3dfba6b0b503d70d21721b5>
        a               sh:NodeShape ;
        rdfs:label      "移动"@zh , "Locomoção"@pt , "Move"@en , "Перемещение"@ru , "Objektbewegung"@de , "Μετακίνηση"@el , "Déplacement"@fr ;
        sh:description  "This class comprises changes of the physical location of the instances of E19 Physical Object.\nNote, that the class E9 Move inherits the property P7 took place at (witnessed): E53 Place. This property should be used to describe the trajectory or a larger area within which a move takes place, whereas the properties P26 moved to (was destination of), P27 moved from (was origin of) describe the start and end points only. Moves may also be documented to consist of other moves (via P9 consists of (forms part of)), in order to describe intermediate stages on a trajectory. In that case, start and end points of the partial moves should match appropriately between each other and with the overall event."@en ;
        sh:name         "Move"@en , "Locomoção"@pt , "Objektbewegung"@de , "Перемещение"@ru , "Déplacement"@fr , "Μετακίνηση"@el , "移动"@zh ;
        sh:nodeKind     sh:IRI ;
